<h1 class="page-title">Permissions</h1>
<p class="page-desc">Who can configure BotNexus, and what each module needs from your server's role setup.</p>

<h2 id="permission-tiers">Permission tiers</h2>
<p>Commands fall into three tiers. Every command page in this documentation tags which tier it belongs to.</p>
<table class="doc-table">
  <tr><th>Tier</th><th>Who</th></tr>
  <tr><td><span class="tag everyone">Everyone</span></td><td>Any member of the server</td></tr>
  <tr><td><span class="tag admin">Admin</span></td><td>Members with Manage Server, or a manager role</td></tr>
  <tr><td><span class="tag owner">Server Owner</span></td><td>The server owner only</td></tr>
</table>

<h2 id="setting-manager-roles">Setting manager roles</h2>
<p>By default, only Administrators can open <code class="inline">/botconfig</code>. To let other staff configure
BotNexus without full admin rights, run <code class="inline">/serversettings</code> and add their role under
<strong>Manager Roles</strong>.</p>

<div class="callout tip">
  <span class="callout-icon">✓</span>
  <p>Manager roles can open every module in <code class="inline">/botconfig</code> except billing and integration
  keys, which stay restricted to Administrators.</p>
</div>

<h2 id="role-hierarchy">Role hierarchy</h2>
<p>BotNexus's own role must sit above any role it assigns or manages — mute roles, level roles, verified roles,
and ticket support roles. If a module isn't applying a role correctly, this is the first thing to check.</p>

